{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"worthless-titanite-bubblefish","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Per-class fallback chains\n\n## Context / Problem\nA class may name a model that is not always reachable — a local endpoint that is down, a provider\nbeing throttled. Today a single unreachable model fails the gate outright; there is no way to say\n\"use the local trivial model, but fall back to a hosted one\".\n\n## Approach\nConsume the `fallback` array that the schema ticket already parses, constructing pydantic-ai's\n`FallbackModel(default, *fallbacks, fallback_on=...)` per class. Fallback entries are INLINE model\nconfigs (same shape as a slot), not references to named presets, so nothing requires the operator to\nlook up rebar vocabulary.\n\n`fallback_on` must be set deliberately rather than left at its default. pydantic-ai's own docs warn\nthat provider SDK retry logic can delay failover substantially — a 429 may be retried inside the SDK\nfor up to ~60s before the fallback is ever reached — so the condition is narrowed to the errors where\nswitching providers actually helps (availability/rate-limit classes), not every exception.\n\n**Alternative rejected — rebar-implemented retry/failover.** pydantic-ai already ships this and rebar\nalready depends on it; a second implementation would diverge from the runner's error taxonomy.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/` — construct `FallbackModel` from a class's fallback list where the model is built.\n- `tests/unit/` — construction and selection tests.\n\n## Testing\nUnit tier with a stubbed model: no network, no live provider.\n- a class with no `fallback` builds the plain model (no FallbackModel wrapper) — today's behaviour.\n- a class with one fallback builds a FallbackModel whose default is the primary.\n- an error in the configured `fallback_on` class selects the fallback.\n- an error OUTSIDE that class propagates instead of silently failing over.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] a test asserts a class without `fallback` builds an unwrapped model (no behaviour change)\n- [ ] a test asserts a class with `fallback` builds a FallbackModel whose default is the primary entry\n- [ ] a test asserts an error in the configured condition selects the fallback entry\n- [ ] a test asserts an error outside the condition PROPAGATES rather than failing over\n- [ ] the chosen `fallback_on` condition is documented in-code with the SDK-retry caveat","id":"cc33-13db-de48-4468","parent_id":"eb58-e71d-ec90-4b00","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Per-class fallback chains"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785470700497085001,"uuid":"9115e8ba-a379-443f-acf7-e2e22de4d54a"}